  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers are expected today into Monday, with best \nchances across Central NY as a slow moving Nor'easter grazes the \narea.\n\nAn anomalously strong coastal low off the New Jersey coast will \ncomplete a cyclonic loop to the south of Long Island today, with the \nlow nearing the Jersey shore this afternoon and tonight. The \nwestward drift of the vertically stacked low will advect Atlantic\nmoisture westward across NY/PA, with increasing clouds. The first\nchance of showers will reach central NY early this morning, then\nprogress gradually westward as an inverted trough axis north of\nthe low center rotates westward. Showers may reach the Genesee \nValley and western Finger Lakes by early to mid afternoon. Far \nwestern New York should stay dry most of the day, although a few\nlight showers should arrive by late afternoon or evening.\n\nThe coastal low is then forecast to slowly meander northeast along \nthe New England coast tonight through Tuesday, weakening with time. \nThe greatest rain chances and greatest western extent of the rain \nshield will be tonight, with showers then gradually tapering off and \nending from west to east late tonight through Monday as the low \nweakens and moves northeast.",
